Question 15.
Briefly explain (in 2-3 sentences) what event flow is in the DOM, and give one example of how event bubbling could affect a shopping cart app like Flipkart.

Answer:
Event flow describes how an event moves through the DOM when an action happens. It has three phases: capturing phase (top to target), target phase (actual element), and bubbling phase (target back to parent elements).

Example: In a Flipkart-style shopping cart app, if a user clicks an "Add to Cart" button inside a product card, the click event can bubble up to the product card or parent container and accidentally trigger another click handler unless it is stopped using event.stopPropagation().

